### ❓ First: Do we need to change TweakLens? Does it accept any port?

**No changes needed! TweakLens already accepts ANY port number.** 

The text box at the top is completely free-form. Whether your terminal gives you `http://localhost:54321`, `http://localhost:3001`, or `http://localhost:9999`, you can paste **any link** into the bar, click **Go**, and TweakLens will load it immediately!

---

# TweakLens Zero-Memory Cheatsheet

## 1. Start TweakLens (Terminal 1)

```powershell
cd C:\DEV\tweaklens
npm run dev
```

---

## 2. Start Your Project (Terminal 2)

Go to your project folder and run the command for your framework.

### Flutter
```powershell
flutter run -d web-server
```
Copy the `http://localhost:XXXXX` link and paste into TweakLens.

### Next.js / Vite / React
```powershell
npm run dev
```
Copy the local link (e.g. `http://localhost:3000`) and paste into TweakLens.

### Expo / React Native Web
```powershell
npx expo start --web
```
Copy the link and paste into TweakLens.

### Python (Streamlit / Flask)
```powershell
streamlit run app.py   # Streamlit
python app.py          # Flask
```
Copy the link and paste into TweakLens.

