## 3. The 2 Modes

| Button | What it does | When to use it |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Test & Click** | Clicks/type pass into your app. | Testing navigation, clicking tabs. |
| **Edit UI Tools** | Visual box drawer + element picker. | Annotating changes for AI. |

---

## 4. The Workflow (Edit Mode)

### Step-by-step

1. Switch to **Edit UI Tools**.
2. Click **Pick Element** — your cursor becomes a crosshair.
3. Click any element in your app (button, text, card, etc).
4. TweakLens **auto-draws a box** over it and captures:
   - Its selector (e.g. `button.subscribe`)
   - Its component name (e.g. `ItemCards`)
   - Its source file (e.g. `src/components/fan-pwa/ItemCards.tsx:97`)
   - Its current styles (color, font, spacing, etc.)
5. In the right sidebar, fill in what you want to change:
   - **Action Type** — Restyle, Move, Insert, or Remove
   - **Text** — what it should say
   - **Color** — what color it should be
   - **Instruction** — any extra detail for the AI
6. Repeat for as many elements as needed.
7. Click **Copy Batch Plan for AI**.
8. Paste into your AI chat (Claude, Cursor, OpenCode, etc).

### Manual alternative (no Pick)

You can also **drag a box** over any element. The box won't auto-capture source info, but you can type the selector or component name by hand in the sidebar.

---

## 5. Exporting to AI

### The prompt includes (automatically)

- Element selectors (`button.subscribe`, `.hero-banner`)
- Component names (`data-tl="ItemCards"`)
- Source file + line (`src/components/.../ItemCards.tsx:97`)
- Current computed styles (before state)
- Your instructions (action, text, color, notes)

### Project rules (toggle ON by default)

The exported prompt includes a **PROJECT RULES** block that tells the AI:
- Follow the repo's AGENTS.md conventions
- Use the existing design system (branding tokens, buttonClass, cardRadius)
- Run typecheck + lint + check-docs after changes
- Make it responsive at all breakpoints

You can uncheck "Include project rules" if you don't need it.

### Where to paste it

| Tool | How |
| :--- | :--- |
| **OpenCode (CLI)** | Paste directly in chat. The AI already has your repo. |
| **Claude / ChatGPT** | Paste the plan + attach the relevant file(s). |
| **Cursor** | Paste in chat. Cursor reads your project files. |
| **Local AI** | Paste only the 1-2 files being edited + the plan. |

---

## 6. Tips

- **Design at multiple viewports** — switch between Mobile / Tablet / Desktop to catch layout issues.
- **Source info is automatic** — if the app is React/Next.js, TweakLens reads the component source. If not, you'll get selectors only (still useful).
- **Rules preamble protects you** — the AI won't hardcode colors or break your design system.
